the Americas, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and the Asia Pacific. It operates through two segments; Hydraulics and Electronics. The Hydraulics segment designs and manufactures hydraulic motion control and fluid conveyance technology products, including cartridge valves, manifolds, and quick release couplings, as well as engineers complete hydraulic system solutions. This segment sells its products under the Sun Hydraulics, Faster, NEM, Taimi, Daman, and Schultes brands. The Electronics segment designs and manufactures customized electronic controls systems, displays, wire harnesses, and software solutions. This segment sells its products under Enovation Controls, Murphy, Zero Off, HCT, Balboa Water Group, i3PD and Cygnus Reach and Joyonway brands. It markets and sells hydraulic products and engineered solutions through value-added distributors, as well as directly to original equipment manufacturers (OEMs); and electronic products to OEMs, distributors, and system integrators. It serves construction, material handling, agriculture, industrial, mobile, energy, recreational vehicles, marine, aerospace, and health and wellness sectors. The company was formerly known as Sun Hydraulics Corporation and changed its name to Helios Technologies, Inc. in June 2019. Helios Technologies, Inc. was incorporated in 1970 and is headquartered in Sarasota, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Sean  Bagan | President, CEO & Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $2.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $365K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers, improving at 10%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $45K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Helios Technologies, Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $1.6B market cap on $839M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -2% over the past three years and +16% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 38%.","The business throws off $104M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 12 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.63\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 15\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.7%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.4pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 23% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Piotroski score 9/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","29 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Financial quality scores above most Industrials peers"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Helios (HLIO) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/helios-hlio-q3-2026-earnings-211414000.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794000916.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Helios projects 2026 sales of $895M-$902M while integrating Radio Sound (NYSE:HLIO)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4668464-helios-projects-2026-sales-of-895m-902m-while-integrating-radio-sound","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793993811.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.318,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Helios Technologies (NYSE:HLIO) Announces FY 2026 Earnings Guidance","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/helios-technologies-nysehlio-announces-fy-2026-earnings-guidance.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793984212.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"HLIO Q3 2026 deep dive: cautious outlook follows strong segment growth and data center entry","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/a